# Flow control

The page is small so that the rules fire on a document short enough to read.
Everything below is a paginator decision, and the trace is where each one
becomes visible.

## Widows and orphans

Two lines of a paragraph are kept together at a boundary, so a single line is
never stranded at the foot of one page or carried alone to the top of the next.
This paragraph runs long on purpose: it has to straddle a break for the rule to
have anything to do, and a shorter one would pass by never being tested.

:::mdv-page{break=avoid}
### Kept together

| Plan | Price |
| --- | --- |
| Team | $19 |
| Business | $49 |
:::

:::mdv-page{break=before}
:::

## After a forced break

A visual block is atomic: it moves to the next page rather than splitting, and
the heading above it goes with it.

```mdv bar
title: Weekly signups
desc: A bar chart of signups for four weeks, rising from 1204 to 1502.
x: week
y: signups
---
week,signups
W-31,1204
W-32,1388
W-33,1291
W-34,1502
```

:::mdv-page{break=after}
:::
